      <transcript>KYLICENGGYI</transcript>
      <definition>n. and adj. Patience", forbearance, indulgence, tolerance; patient," indulgent, tolerant.</definition>
      <page>499</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠺᠥᠯᠢᠴᠡᠩᠺᠥᠢ ᠡᠴᠡ ᠢᠯᠡᠭᠦᠦ ᠪᠤᠶᠠᠨ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ ᠺᠢᠯᠢᠩ ᠡᠴᠡ ᠢᠯᠡᠭᠦᠦ ᠺᠢᠯᠢᠨᠴᠡ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- ece ilegyy bujan ygei, kiling ece ilegyy kilince ygei</transcript>
          <definition>; There is no greater virtue than patience, there is no greater sin than anger ( proverb).</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠺᠥᠯᠢᠴᠡᠩᠺᠥᠢ ᠺᠦᠮᠦᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- kymyn‘</transcript>
          <definition>A patient person</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠺᠥᠯᠢᠴᠡᠩᠺᠥᠢ ᠰᠡᠳᠺᠢᠯᠲᠦ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- sedkilty</transcript>
          <definition>Patient, forbearing, tolerant, indulgent</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠺᠥᠯᠢᠴᠡᠩᠺᠥᠢ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- ygei</transcript>
          <definition>Unbearable, intolerable</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
